the European Union's General Affairs  Council is due to set this week a date  for Serbia to start at CU membership  negotiations the minister's must choose  a day that falls before the end of  January to launch the process which will  see Serbia negotiate the 35 policy areas  or chapters candidates must complete  before they can join they'll also assess  Albania's request for candidate status  and the former Republic of Macedonia  hopes of beginning accession talks as  part of a broader look at the EU  enlargement process the council is also  set to debate a review of the European  external action service talks will focus  on some recommendations that could be  implemented in the short term notably  boosting cooperation between EU  delegations and those of the Member  States and improving the effectiveness  of common security and defence policy  missions The ministers will also discuss  preparations for the European Council on  the nineteenth and twentieth of December  in Brussels EU leaders are set to  discuss defence policy and Europe's  defence industry economic policy and  progress on completing the banking Union  the fate of would-be immigrants in the  Mediterranean and relations with Ukraine  and the Central African Republic
 

